      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Exercise: depth map to 3D point cloud\n\nTakes a depth map (from any source) and back-projects to a colored 3D point cloud using camera intrinsics:\n1. Load depth as BGR float32, extract channel 0 (no weighted formula).\n2. 'CV Depth to 3D Points' computes X=(u-cx)*Z/fx, Y=-(v-cy)*Z/fy.\n3. 'CV Write PLY' exports the cloud for PreviewPointCloud.\n\nImages: NYU Depth V2 sample 10 (indoor hallway, 1-9.5 m depth).\n  Dataset: https://huggingface.co/datasets/jagennath-hari/nyuv2\n  Camera intrinsics: https://huggingface.co/datasets/jagennath-hari/nyuv2/blob/main/camera_params.json\ndepth_scale converts raw float 0-1 to meters: 65535/1000 = 65.535."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
